Another important method for jet quenching is the high \(p_{\rm T}\) hadron-hadron azimuthal correlation. In different collisions systems( p+p, d+A and Au+Au) from the STAR experiments, shown on Fig. 1.8, from this plots, the flavor dependent medium interaction can be obtained, for the triggered particles, there is a minimum \(p_{\rm T}\) cuts required, those particles's parents partons are created mostly in the initial hard scatterings in the early stage. the created pair of partons go through the medium in opposite directions in the transverse plane. In Fig. 1.8, there is a clear peak on the away side (\(\Delta\phi=\pi\)), \(\Delta\phi\) is calculated based on the Eq. 1.5, in both p+p and d+Au collisions. However, peak disappeared in central Au+Au collisions, this can be explained as one of the partons loses all of its energy in the hot QCD medium. In Au+Au collisions, due to strong

