#### Collective motion

In semi-central or peripheral Au+Au collisions, the overlapping area of two ions is an ellipsoid shape, which will lead to the spatial space asymmetry and will be transferred into the momentum space asymmetry by the asymmetry of pressure gradients which is shown on 1.9.

Figure 1.8: Comparison of two particles azimuthal distributions for central d+Au collisions to those seen in p+p and central Au+Au collisions. The respective pedestals have been subtracted.

The final state particles production can be expanded in a form of fourier series Eq.6 azimuthal particle distributions in momentum space. The coefficient \(v_{n}\) of the fourier series Eq. 6 can be found in the Eq. 7.

\[E\frac{d^{3}N}{d\vec{p}^{3}}=\frac{1}{2\pi}\frac{d^{2}N}{p_{T}dp_{T}dy}\{1+\sum _{i=1}^{\infty}2v_{n}\cos[n(\phi-\Psi_{r})]\} \tag{6}\]

\[v_{n}=<cos[n(\phi-\Phi_{RP})]> \tag{7}\]

