#### Heavy Flavor Tracker (HFT)

The Heavy Flavor Tracker (HFT) is a new silicon detector designed to improve heavy flavor measurement precision [56, 57]. It can reconstruct open charm hadrons, such as \(D^{0}\), \(D^{\ast}\) and \(\Lambda_{c}\)[58, 59], via the reconstruction of their secondary decay vertices through the hadronic decays channels. The HFT can also measure the bottom production by an indirect way, through the non-photonic electrons, non-prompt J/\(\psi\), non-prompt \(D^{0}\)[60].

